{"id": "EUVD-2026-80477", "enisaUuid": "f7c83721-5f5c-3125-9aa2-27f971490dec", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmedia: saa7164: fix cleanup on resource allocation failure\n\nsaa7164_dev_setup() adds the device to the global saa7164_devlist before\nrequesting the PCI BAR memory regions.\n\nIf get_resources() fails, saa7164_dev_setup() decrements the device count\nand returns an error, but leaves the device on saa7164_devlist. The probe\nerror path then frees the device, leaving a dangling entry on the global\nlist.\n\nReuse the existing MMIO mapping error path to remove the device from\nsaa7164_devlist and decrement the device count before returning.\n\nAlso release BAR0 if it was successfully requested but the BAR2 request\nfails.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:31:44", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:54:10", "baseScore": 8.4, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/daa5b32cdf7db81a07ee2a91ce092a363e7754aa", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/77f216f8de6221efb6f6c471bc9e598f1879825b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/69259c627009bf7621010ae9e997dad2dad3339c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4d2048466af9e2c960c5be6dcd317e3b657d268b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fc65623524b5bf23baddc6ae688d954fba0d5de2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/28e84c6e2e6753ed238ea097b2842a32a6a6879b"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89877", "GHSA-33q9-xpr9-fmxv"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "081590cf-426d-343d-a98b-e9a8c92fefce", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "443c1228d50518f3c550e1fef490a2c9d9246ce7 <daa5b32cdf7db81a07ee2a91ce092a363e7754aa"}, {"id": "19dfa2db-ad38-328f-aded-f3a980314ec2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "23a857bf-a1e8-3f8c-aee8-9da6de20aa99", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.32"}, {"id": "2e091e9a-21ad-37f3-b536-6352ba7e08e6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.51"}, {"id": "307530f7-047c-370a-bd57-f30372c33ccc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "3bfca6b6-04b0-3266-a1bd-3405d98c4d74", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "58a93614-7104-31eb-b19b-2f836cc51af0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "443c1228d50518f3c550e1fef490a2c9d9246ce7 <77f216f8de6221efb6f6c471bc9e598f1879825b"}, {"id": "58cf9d21-2481-3df9-8a57-8afd9ab8201e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "597e47d7-3e51-3f84-a7ba-3445a23193e2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "443c1228d50518f3c550e1fef490a2c9d9246ce7 <4d2048466af9e2c960c5be6dcd317e3b657d268b"}, {"id": "6bd6ec7b-36a7-392f-9154-6339eba65609", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "443c1228d50518f3c550e1fef490a2c9d9246ce7 <28e84c6e2e6753ed238ea097b2842a32a6a6879b"}, {"id": "8d375390-428a-39ae-a9b5-3e1a586ff7a8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}, {"id": "bebd3294-a14e-3179-a91d-bb15beb7aff1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "443c1228d50518f3c550e1fef490a2c9d9246ce7 <69259c627009bf7621010ae9e997dad2dad3339c"}, {"id": "e08d3109-275c-32f8-87a1-e1580d0b45af", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "443c1228d50518f3c550e1fef490a2c9d9246ce7 <fc65623524b5bf23baddc6ae688d954fba0d5de2"}, {"id": "ef0d3bea-db1c-3c34-9e0b-d0f1fab13fdd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "6